{
 "title": "Fix duplicate batches on CSV import retry",
 "mode": "implement",
 "created": "2026-10-10T19:04:56+00:00",
 "criteria": [
  {
   "id": "AC1",
   "text": "With a transient \"database is locked\" failure injected right after a batch's rows are written (`IMPORTER_FAULTS=progress:1`) and `--retries 3`, `python -m importer import samples/products.csv --batch-size 2` exits 0 and the database holds each batch exactly once: 5 records, batch_no counts 2/2/1, and `importer list` shows batches=3 rows=5 stored=5",
   "proof": "e2e",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T19:05:17+00:00"
  },
  {
   "id": "AC2",
   "text": "A sloppy real-world file (UTF-8 BOM, CRLF line endings, padded cells; and the `.tsv` variant) imported under the same transient failure also stores each row exactly once",
   "proof": "e2e",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T19:05:17+00:00"
  },
  {
   "id": "R1",
   "text": "An import with no failures behaves as before: exit 0, prints `import <id>: 5 rows in 3 batches`, 5 records stored, `list` counters match",
   "proof": "e2e",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T19:05:17+00:00"
  },
  {
   "id": "R2",
   "text": "`import FILE --dry-run` still prints `dry run: <n> rows in <m> batches, nothing written` and creates no database file",
   "proof": "e2e",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T19:05:17+00:00"
  },
  {
   "id": "R3",
   "text": "The CLI keeps its flags: `import FILE [--db] [--retries N] [--batch-size N] [--dry-run]` and `list [--db]` are accepted exactly as before",
   "proof": "e2e",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T19:05:17+00:00"
  },
  {
   "id": "R4",
   "text": "A file with a bad row still stops with exit 2 and `error: line <n>: bad row ...`, marks the import `failed`, and keeps the batches before the bad row stored once (added by trace: same error path in cmd_import)",
   "proof": "e2e",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T19:06:03+00:00"
  }
 ],
